libstdc++ 13 <sstream>: `o << 4' left o.str() empty: the specializations of
basic_ostream<char>::_M_insert are declared `extern template' in
bits/ostream.tcc and were not instantiated.  Such member declarations are
now discarded ([temp.explicit]/12,
cpp98_explicit_instantiation_of_member_function_template/test_cpp11.desc),
and the num_put and numpunct facets of the "C" locale, which libstdc++.so
provides, are modelled ([locale.general]/8,
cpp11_ostream_integer_insertion_classic_locale).  g++ 13 accepts this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
